From John Zhang <jzhang@jimmy.harvard.edu>  Thu Jul 11 16:42:43 2002
From: John Zhang <jzhang@jimmy.harvard.edu> (John Zhang)
Date: Thu, 11 Jul 2002 11:42:43 -0400 (EDT)
Subject: [BioC] Alert: Up coming changes to annotate
Message-ID: <200207111542.LAA23190@blaise.dfci.harvard.edu>

Changes to the annotate package is expected to take place in two weeks that will 
involve removing all the data files for Affymetrix chips that are currectly in 
the data subdirectory of annotate. 

If your code relies on those data files, please consider using the data packages 
that can be downloaded from Bioconductor under Downloads and then Data where you 
will find annotation data for various Affymetrix chips in the format of data 
packages and XML files. A data package can be installed and loaded as any R 
packages. Typing packageName() (e. g. hgu95a()) after the package has been 
loaded will list all the rda files for that data package. Each rda file in the 
data subdirectory of a given data package is an R environment with key and value 
pairs. Data in each rda file can be accessed using operations that are 
applicable to an R environment object.

The current version of annotate will be made available afterwards but the data 
files will not be updated.

Please contact me if you have any concern.


